---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/beauty';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for/beauty');
const desc = description(site, 'for/beauty');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How should beauty brands time replenishment?",
    "answer": "Use pack size, customer usage and observed one-time reorder intervals to form a range. Check recent purchases and current subscription state before sending; there is no universal beauty reminder delay."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should sample buyers receive full-bottle offers immediately?",
    "answer": "First establish interest in the samples and help with access to product guidance. A proposed preference-based follow-up is more informative than assuming every sample buyer wants the same bottle."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a subscription integration prove skip recovery works?",
    "answer": "No. Confirm that the specific connector exposes pause, skip and next-shipment changes and that queued messages recheck those states."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should the tool demonstration prove?",
    "answer": "Show routine education, preference correction, multi-item purchase handling and suppression after a new order or scheduled shipment using your own catalog."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which costs should be compared?",
    "answer": "Compare current supplier quotes for the same contacts and sends, connector work, implementation, maintenance and optional channels. No fixed prices or universal winner are established here."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/for">← All store types</a>
    <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Beauty brands</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Choose Shopify email tools for beauty routines</h1>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2>Start with the product routine</h2>
      <p>Beauty merchants need to distinguish a repeat purchase from an automatic subscription shipment, a sample from a full-size product, and a preference from a permanent customer attribute. Choose an email tool by whether it can represent those distinctions in your actual catalog. This is a selection framework, not a tested ranking or a promise of higher retention.</p>
      <p>Build a record for each routine: product and variant purchased, quantity, delivery date, expected usage range, subscription state and the next appropriate instruction. A moisturizer and an occasional hair treatment should not inherit one universal replenishment delay. Ask customers about usage where helpful; purchase intervals alone also reflect gifts, promotions and stockpiling.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2>Replenishment and subscription suppression</h2>
      <p>Estimate days of supply from pack quantity and plausible usage, then compare that estimate with observed reorder intervals for one-time buyers. Treat the estimate as uncertain. Offer an easy way to say that the product is still in use rather than repeatedly insisting that it is empty. Account for shipping lead time without inventing a universal reminder window.</p>
      <p>Shopify supports recurring purchase options through its own or third-party subscription apps. That does not establish that an email provider receives skip, pause or next-charge events. Before enabling reminders, demonstrate an active subscriber, a paused subscriber, a changed shipment date and a one-time buyer in the proposed integration. Recheck state immediately before sending so a newly scheduled shipment can suppress a redundant sales prompt.</p>
      <p>A skip confirmation belongs with the system that owns the subscription action. Optional routine advice can follow when relevant, but a skip is not proof of dissatisfaction. Pantry-like product accumulation, travel and changed usage call for different responses. Do not turn every pause into a discount sequence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2>Shade, scent and education paths</h2>
      <p>For hair color, preserve the purchased shade and product system, then ask whether the customer wants technique guidance or a different result. A past purchase may have been for someone else. Let shoppers revise preferences; avoid treating a quiz answer as a medical diagnosis or evidence that a formulation is suitable for them.</p>
      <p>For fragrance, separate a discovery-set purchase from a full-bottle purchase. A proposed journey asks which samples the customer preferred before presenting a related bottle. Do not impose a purported universal wear-test duration. For nail products, compatibility instructions should come from approved product guidance rather than a recommendation inferred solely from color.</p>
      <p>Publish ingredient, use and storage information approved for the actual item. Email can link to that guidance and support; it should not invent efficacy claims. Send the routine instructions before a bundle offer when the customer still needs help using the original purchase.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2>Which tools belong in the shortlist?</h2>
      <p>Include Sequenzy if you want to evaluate assisted workflow creation, but require a demonstration with your product identifiers and subscription events. An appealing generated sequence is insufficient if its suppression cannot read the current subscription state. Confirm supported integration, operator review, rollback and current commercial terms directly; this guide does not establish those capabilities.</p>
      <p>Compare Klaviyo and Omnisend using the same beauty cases rather than assigning either an order-volume threshold. Ask each to show a preference update, a multi-item order and a subscriber whose next shipment changes after entering a replenishment flow. Compare how much custom event work and ongoing maintenance your team would own. Drip can be another candidate for a team evaluating explicit branching; demonstrate the branches rather than assuming all required events exist.</p>
      <p>Keep review and loyalty systems distinct from the sending platform. Yotpo Email & SMS has been decommissioned, so it is not a current email shortlist option. Existing review or loyalty arrangements require their own integration assessment; retaining those products does not restore the retired sender.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise and costs</h2>
      <p>Use staff-controlled records for a sample buyer, a full-size one-time buyer and an active subscriber. Queue routine education and a replenishment offer, then simulate a new order, a paused shipment and a preference correction. Confirm the intended message changes or stops, and that an operator can explain why. This is a proposed exercise; no merchant trial or conversion improvement is claimed here.</p>
      <p>Price the same actual contact population, expected sends, SMS usage if needed, subscription connector and implementation work with every supplier. Include the cost of repairing incorrect joins between products, variants and subscriptions. Large quiz lists do not by themselves prove that one billing model is cheaper.</p>
      <p>Report reorder rate by product and one-time versus subscription status, education-related support questions, opt-outs and net contribution after discounts and returns. Attribute cautiously: a scheduled subscriber shipment is not evidence that a reminder caused a purchase. A randomized comparison, where appropriate and sufficiently sized, can estimate incremental impact.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Documentation and next steps</h2><p>Primary documentation checked 24 November 2026. Documentation establishes only the stated product behavior; account configuration and the proposed workflows still need verification.</p><ul><li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/products/purchase-options/subscriptions">Shopify subscriptions</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications">Shopify store notifications</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo decommission notice</a></li></ul><p><a class="link" href="/apps">Explore the tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/for">Compare store requirements</a></p></div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Beauty brands email FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
